WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Say «petit». Small.

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.340
The T is silent.

3
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.660
Now add one letter: «petite».

4
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.770
Suddenly you hear the T.

5
00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.730
Then «petits» and «petites».

6
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.190
Four spellings. English
needs just one word:

7
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:20.430
small. So why does French need
four spellings for one small word?

8
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.760
And can your ears tell them all apart?

9
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.520
In this mission, you'll
fill a four-box grid,

10
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.690
with one form of «petit» in each box.

11
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.740
Then you'll flip a switch in the lab,

12
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.850
and predict what «heureux»
and «génial» do next.

13
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.040
Your mission: work out
why one word like 'small'

14
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.120
takes four forms in French.
